@@ -2,6 +2,26 @@

 JSON in, JSON out. Routes are listed in `README.md`.

+## Keys and roles
+
+Every request sends `Authorization: Bearer <key>`. Keys are kept in the data
+as `apiKeys: [{ "key", "name", "role" }]`; `data/seed.json` has one per role.
+
+- `viewer` may only read (`GET`), except `GET /audit`.
+- `cook` may also `POST /recipes/:id/cook`, `POST /batches/:id/waste`,
+  `POST /temperatures` and `POST /stocktakes/:id/counts`.
+- `manager` may do everything, including `GET /audit`.
+
+No key, or a key that is not known, is `401 unauthorized`; a known key
+without the role for the route is `403 forbidden`.
+
+## Audit
+
+Every request that may change data (any method but `GET`) by a known key
+writes an audit entry `{ id, at, keyName, method, path, status }`, whatever
+its outcome (refused and failed requests included). `GET /audit` lists them
+newest first, for managers only. Entries name the key, never the key itself.
+
 ## Errors

 Errors have a status from `src/errors.js` and the body
